# CHANGELOG.md is written only when a release is cut — day-to-day entries go in
# `changelog.d/` as one file per change, so branches never edit the same lines.
# See changelog.d/README.md.
#
# The union merge stays for the branches still carrying CHANGELOG.md edits, and
# for release-time merges. Note it only helps LOCALLY: GitHub's server-side
# merge ignores .gitattributes merge drivers, which is why every pull request
# used to show a CHANGELOG conflict despite this line.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
